,title,link,text,language,family
0,Dinka people - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinka_people,"The Dinka people (Dinka: Jiɛ̈ɛ̈ŋ) are a Nilotic ethnic group native to South Sudan. The Dinka mostly live along the Nile, from Mangalla-Bor [1] to Renk, in the region of Bahr el Ghazal, Upper Nile (two out of three provinces that were formerly part of southern Sudan), and the Abyei area of the Ngok Dinka in South Sudan.","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
1,Dinka people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinka_people,"The Dinka people (Dinka: Jiɛ̈ɛ̈ŋ) are a Nilotic ethnic group native to South Sudan. The Dinka mostly live along the Nile, from Mangalla-Bor [1] to Renk, in the region of Bahr el Ghazal, Upper Nile (two out of three provinces that were formerly part of southern Sudan), and the Abyei area of the Ngok Dinka in South Sudan.","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
