4,Dinka Songs from South Sudan Collection - Ambientscape,https://ambientscape.com/dinka,"Dinka Songs from South Sudan British Library Collection The songs in this collection were recorded for a project conducted between 2009 and 2012 by researchers from the University of Edinburgh and the School of Oriental and African Studies, University of London, in collaboration with Dinka researchers in South Sudan.","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
5,A Collection of Dinka Songs - University of Edinburgh ...Dinka Music - MelodiggingA Collection of Dinka Songs,https://www.research.ed.ac.uk/en/datasets/a-collection-of-dinka-songs/,"In this context, we aimed to record a large collection of Dinka songs for preservation in a long-term sound archive. This collection is the result of that effort. It presents song material from 36 Dinka singers and groups of singers. Dinka music is the traditional vocal- and rhythm-centered music of the Dinka (Jieng) people of South Sudan. It is predominantly collective and participatory, built around a lead singer who cues a chorus in call-and-response, supported by handclaps, foot-stomps, ululations, and simple percussion. The songs in this collection were recorded and annotated as part of the project 'Metre and Melody in Dinka Speech and Song', a project carried out by researchers from the University of Edinburgh and the School of Oriental and African Studies in London, and funded by the UK Arts and Humanities Research Council as part of their 'Beyond Text' programme. The project aimed to understand the ...","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
6,Dinka Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/dinka-music,"Dinka music is the traditional vocal- and rhythm-centered music of the Dinka (Jieng) people of South Sudan. It is predominantly collective and participatory, built around a lead singer who cues a chorus in call-and-response, supported by handclaps, foot-stomps, ululations, and simple percussion.","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
7,A Collection of Dinka Songs,https://datashare.is.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/155,"The songs in this collection were recorded and annotated as part of the project 'Metre and Melody in Dinka Speech and Song', a project carried out by researchers from the University of Edinburgh and the School of Oriental and African Studies in London, and funded by the UK Arts and Humanities Research Council as part of their 'Beyond Text' programme. The project aimed to understand the ...","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
8,Dinka Traditional Songs: Celebrating South Sudan's Vibrant Culture,https://nativetribes.blog/blog/dinka-traditional-songs-celebrating-south,"Dinka traditional songs are the lifeblood of the Dinka people, one of South Sudan's largest ethnic groups. These songs aren't just for entertainment; they're deeply woven into the fabric of daily life.","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
9,"Music of the Sudan: The Role of Song and Dance in Dinka Society, Vol. 1 ...",https://folkways.si.edu/music-of-the-sudan-the-role-of-song-and-dance-in-dinka-society-album-one-war-songs-and-hymns/islamica-world/album/smithsonian,"Here is an opportunity to explore two genres of traditional song from the Dinka tribes of southern Sudan. War songs speak to the Dinka’s courage and ferocity, although the singers claim they are never aggressors. Hymns","Dinka, South Central",Nilo-Saharan
